-- 310: KAIST Scholarship for International Graduate Students (rel 9)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'KAIST Scholarship for International Graduate Students', provider = 'KAIST (Korea Advanced Institute of Science & Technology)', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No separate scholarship deadline: select the KAIST Scholarship option inside the KAIST international graduate admission application (three admission periods a year - Spring, Fall Early and Fall Regular).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's","PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The KAIST Scholarship is KAIST's scholarship program designed for international graduate students: applicants select the KAIST Scholarship option in the international graduate admission application (Spring, Fall Early and Fall Regular admission periods; all departments except the Global Technology Innovation Program's GDI-GTIP track), and it currently benefits the great majority (94%) of KAIST's international student body. It provides full tuition coverage, national health insurance support and a monthly stipend whose level depends on the student's research involvement, and is often complemented by laboratory research support so that most recipients can be financially self-sufficient; KAIST's application guides note that coverage varies by individual and that recipients' performance is reviewed for continuation. Two prestigious tiers sit on top of the base scholarship, for which accepted KAIST Scholarship candidates are automatically considered without a separate procedure: the KAIST Global Presidential Scholarship (KGPS), for Master's and Master's-Ph.D. integrated students recommended as highly competitive, pays full tuition plus a monthly stipend of KRW 1,000,000 for four regular semesters; and the KAIST Prestige Scholarship (KPS), for Master's-Ph.D. integrated and Ph.D. students, pays full tuition plus KRW 300,000 per month for eight regular semesters (for integrated students it begins at the start of the Ph.D. program). Scholarship decisions are announced with the admission results.$desc$, requirements = $req$Open to international applicants (citizenship outside Korea; Korean dual citizens are not eligible for KAIST international admission) to KAIST Master's, Master's-Ph.D. integrated and Ph.D. programs, holding or expecting the relevant prior degree. Applicants choose the KAIST Scholarship as their financial resource in the online admission application; awardees and rates are decided on prior performance and future promise and announced with the final admission results, and KAIST reviews beneficiaries' performance for continuation of the aid. No numeric GPA cutoff for the scholarship is published and the admission English-proficiency table (e.g. IELTS 6.5 overall band in the 2024 guide) is an admission requirement rather than a scholarship cutoff, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship', source_url = 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship', application_url = 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (cleanup pass 105). The previously stored URL (admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/sub0302) is dead, and the current official KAIST Scholarship page (admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship) returned HTTP 500 to our fetcher on repeated attempts on 2026-10-26 although the page is live and search-indexed. Reliability 9 (not 10) for that reason: the current structure - full tuition, national health insurance and a research-involvement-dependent monthly stipend for the base KAIST Scholarship, with automatic consideration for the KGPS (KRW 1,000,000/month x 4 semesters, Master's/integrated) and KPS (KRW 300,000/month x 8 semesters, Ph.D.) tiers - was read from the search-indexed excerpt of that official URL and corroborated by KAIST's official 2024 Spring International Graduate Admission Application Guide, fetched first-hand (Financial Aid section: full tuition and fees, advisor/program-supported stipend and health-insurance premium, coverage varies by individual, yearly performance review; the guide's flat 2024 stipend figures were deliberately NOT carried over because the current page restructures the stipend by research involvement). Title normalised to the scheme's official name with its graduate scope; degree_levels corrected (the stored URL and scheme are graduate-only - the previous record wrongly included Bachelor's; KAIST's separate undergraduate scholarship is not this record). award_amount NULL (variable): the base stipend varies by research involvement and the KGPS/KPS tiers carry different rates and durations. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (admission-linked across Spring/Fall Early/Fall Regular) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 527 synced; source 2549 repointed from the bare domain to the current official scholarship page.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Full tuition coverage + national health insurance + monthly stipend dependent on research involvement; prestigious tiers KGPS (KRW 1,000,000/month for 4 semesters) and KPS (KRW 300,000/month for 8 semesters) on automatic consideration', tuition_coverage = 'Full tuition coverage for international graduate students (all departments except the GDI-GTIP track), continued subject to performance review.', english_requirements = 'English proficiency must be evidenced for KAIST international graduate admission (the 2024 guide table: IELTS 6.5 overall band, TOEFL iBT 83, TOEIC 720 or TEPS 326, unless waived); the scholarship itself publishes no separate cutoff.', required_documents = $j$["KAIST international graduate admission application selecting the KAIST Scholarship as financial resource","Degree certificates and academic transcripts","English proficiency test score (unless waived)","Recommendation letters (uploaded directly by referees)","Statement of purpose and list of honours and awards"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Three admission periods a year - Spring, Fall (Early) and Fall (Regular); select the KAIST Scholarship option inside the admission application; scholarship decisions are announced with the admission results"}]$json$ WHERE id = 310;

-- 317: Yonsei Global Leader Fellowship (rel 9)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Yonsei Global Leader Fellowship', provider = 'Yonsei University Graduate School', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No separate scholarship deadline: outstanding new international students are recommended by their College/School at graduate admission (Spring and Fall intakes).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's","PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Global Leader Fellowship is Yonsei University Graduate School's top scholarship for outstanding newly admitted international students, awarded on the recommendation of the student's College/School. It covers the full entrance and tuition fees plus a stipend for the regular duration of the degree - four semesters for Master's and Ph.D. students and six semesters for joint (combined Master's-Ph.D.) degree students - provided the fellow maintains a GPA of at least 3.4 out of 4.3 in each semester; if the GPA falls below the minimum, the grant is stopped. It sits above Yonsei's semester-by-semester Outstanding International Student Scholarships (I: full entrance and tuition for one semester; II: 50% for one semester; III: 50% for the regular semesters on departmental financial support), which are separate awards. The Graduate School's official scholarship table does not state the fellowship's stipend amount, so no monthly figure is recorded for it here; scholarships at Yonsei are generally disbursed through the colleges as reductions on tuition bills or to the student's registered bank account.$desc$, requirements = $req$Open to outstanding new international students admitted to Yonsei University Graduate School (Master's, Ph.D. and combined programs) who are recommended by their College/School; there is no separate open application round published for the fellowship. Fellows must maintain a minimum GPA of 3.4/4.3 each semester to remain in the fellowship - a retention condition rather than an entry cutoff - and the scheme publishes no entry GPA or IELTS figure, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do', source_url = 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do', application_url = 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (cleanup pass 105) from Yonsei Graduate School's official 'Special scholarship for Int'l' page fetched the same day (the previously stored scholarships URL is dead). The table entry for the Global Leader Fellowship - outstanding new international students recommended by College/School; full entrance & tuition fee plus stipend; Master's & PhD 4 semesters, joint degree 6 semesters; minimum GPA 3.4/4.3 to remain - was read first-hand, as was the Graduate School's scholarship-guide page on disbursement. Reliability 9 (not 10): the official table does not publish the stipend's amount (a 2021 guideline figure seen in search results was deliberately not carried over as stale), so award_amount is NULL (variable) and the stipend is described rather than quantified. Title corrected to the official singular 'Global Leader Fellowship' (previously stored as 'Global Leaders'). deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (admission-linked recommendation; Spring/Fall intakes) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (3.4/4.3 is a retention rule). Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 513 synced; source 2775 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Full entrance and tuition fees + stipend (amount set by the Graduate School) for the regular semesters', tuition_coverage = 'Full entrance and tuition fees for 4 semesters (Master''s/PhD) or 6 semesters (joint degree), subject to maintaining GPA of at least 3.4/4.3 each semester.', english_requirements = 'Language proficiency is evidenced under Yonsei Graduate School admission rules; the fellowship page publishes no separate IELTS cutoff.', required_documents = $j$["Yonsei Graduate School admission application","Recommendation by the admitting College/School","Academic transcripts and certificates evidencing outstanding record"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Spring and Fall intakes; outstanding new international students are recommended by their College/School at admission - no separate fellowship round"}]$json$ WHERE id = 317;

-- 321: Korea University Global Leader Scholarship (Graduate) (rel 10)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Korea University Global Leader Scholarship (Graduate)', provider = 'Korea University Graduate School', coverage_type = 'Tuition Waiver + Living Support', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No separate scholarship application or deadline: admission and scholarship evaluations are conducted automatically and simultaneously when you apply for Korea University Graduate School admission (Spring and Fall intakes).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's","PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Global Leader Scholarship (Scholarship Type A) is the top tier of the Korea University Graduate School Scholarship for International Students, the Graduate School's admission-linked scholarship family for new international Master's and doctoral students. There is no separate application: the admission evaluation and the scholarship award evaluation are conducted automatically and simultaneously, recipients are chosen by relative evaluation (department recommendation and the Dean's permission), and an applicant assessed for one type may be awarded a different type. Type A - the Global Leader Scholarship - waives 100% of the entrance fee and tuition fee and pays a living support fee of KRW 500,000 per month for the four months of the semester; the other tiers are the Humanities and Social Sciences Scholarship (Type B, 60% of tuition) and the Natural Science and Engineering Scholarship (Type C, 65% of tuition). Importantly, these benefits apply only to the first semester after enrollment: from the second semester, students must apply and be selected for scholarships each semester, with selection based on their KU GPA. The scholarships cannot be held together with the Global Korea Scholarship (GKS) or foundation scholarships, international students in the College of Medicine can only receive Type C, and Business Analytics (Business Administration) applicants are not eligible.$desc$, requirements = $req$International applicants to Korea University Graduate School Master's/doctoral programs who meet all three published conditions for their type are evaluated automatically at admission. Global Leader Scholarship (Type A): cumulative GPA from the previous (latest) school of at least 4.0/4.5, 3.83/4.3, 3.57/4.0 or 90/100; a language score of TOEFL iBT 90+, New TEPS 386+, Academic IELTS 7.0+ or TOPIK level 6; and department recommendation with the Dean's permission. Types B/C: GPA at least 3.5/4.5, 3.36/4.3, 3.14/4.0 or 85/100, and TOEFL iBT 82+, New TEPS 337+, Academic IELTS 6.0+ or TOPIK level 4+. An original test score is mandatory even for native English speakers and those who studied in English-speaking countries; TOEFL Home Edition and IELTS Indicator are not accepted. Because the GPA bar is published as equivalents across four scales and the language bar as one of four alternative tests (with different IELTS figures per type), no single scale-unambiguous figure is stored - min_gpa/min_ielts are NULL and the thresholds are recorded here and in english_requirements.$req$, website_url = 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html', source_url = 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html', application_url = 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (cleanup pass 105) from the Korea University Graduate School's official scholarships page fetched the same day (the previously stored global.do URL returns a service error). The requirements table for Types A/B/C (four-scale GPA equivalents, TOEFL/New TEPS/IELTS/TOPIK bars, all-three-conditions rule, relative evaluation), the automatic simultaneous evaluation, the first-semester-only scope of the benefits with semesterly re-selection, the no-duplication rule with GKS/foundation scholarships, the College of Medicine (Type C only) and Business Analytics exclusions, and the benefits table (A: 100% entrance+tuition and KRW 500,000/month living support for 4 months; B: 60% tuition; C: 65% tuition) were all read first-hand. Title corrected to the official scheme name ('Fellowship' -> 'Scholarship', with its graduate scope; Korea University runs a distinct undergraduate scheme of a similar name). award_amount NULL (variable): the awarded type is decided by relative evaluation and benefits differ by type, so no single figure is stored. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (automatic at admission; Spring/Fall) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL (multi-scale/multi-test thresholds). Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 514 synced; source 2556 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Type A (Global Leader): 100% of entrance fee and tuition fee + living support fee of KRW 500,000/month for 4 months; Type B: 60% of tuition; Type C: 65% of tuition (first semester; semesterly re-selection afterwards)', tuition_coverage = 'Type A waives 100% of the entrance and tuition fees for the first semester; Types B and C waive 60% and 65% of tuition respectively for the first semester. From the second semester students must re-apply and are selected by GPA each semester.', english_requirements = 'A language score is a formal scholarship criterion - Type A: TOEFL iBT 90+, New TEPS 386+, Academic IELTS 7.0+ or TOPIK level 6; Types B/C: TOEFL iBT 82+, New TEPS 337+, Academic IELTS 6.0+ or TOPIK level 4+ (original score mandatory; TOEFL Home Edition and IELTS Indicator not accepted).', required_documents = $j$["Korea University Graduate School admission application (the scholarship is evaluated automatically and simultaneously - no separate application)","Transcript evidencing the cumulative GPA of the previous (latest) school","Original language test score - TOEFL iBT, New TEPS, Academic IELTS or TOPIK (mandatory even for native English speakers)"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Spring and Fall intakes; evaluated automatically with the Graduate School admission application - no separate scholarship application or deadline"}]$json$ WHERE id = 321;

-- 452: Hanyang International Scholarship Program (HISP) (rel 9)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'Hanyang International Scholarship Program (HISP)', provider = 'Hanyang University', coverage_type = 'Tuition Waiver', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No separate application or deadline: HISP grantees are selected during the international admission process (Spring and Fall semesters); the 100-scale GPA certificate must be submitted within the official application period.', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Bachelor","Master's","PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$The Hanyang International Scholarship Program (HISP) is Hanyang University's flagship merit scholarship for newly admitted international students: applicants with excellent grades at their previously attended institution are selected on overall scholastic achievement during the admission process, with no separate application. Qualification requires a GPA of at least 80 when converted to a 100-point scale, and applicants who do not submit the certificate of GPA converted to the 100 scale or percentage within the official application period are not eligible. The benefit comes in three tiers: HISP 100% reduces tuition and admission fees in full, while HISP 70% and HISP 50% reduce tuition by those percentages. For graduate students the scholarship period is four semesters for Master's, four semesters for Ph.D. and six semesters for combined Master's-Ph.D. programs (excluding extended study periods and research registration), and recipients must achieve a minimum GPA of 3.0 each semester to retain it; for undergraduates Hanyang's admission guidelines set the period at eight semesters for freshmen and four for transfer students. The number of grantees may differ every semester, and HISP cannot be combined with other on-campus scholarships.$desc$, requirements = $req$Open to international applicants admitted to Hanyang University undergraduate and graduate degree programs (Seoul and ERICA campuses) whose GPA from the previously attended institution is 80 or higher when converted to a 100-point scale; submission of the 100-scale/percentage GPA certificate during the official application period is mandatory for HISP consideration. Grantees are selected during admission screening without a separate application and must maintain at least a 3.0 GPA each semester (graduate guideline) to keep the award. The 80-point qualification bar sits on a 100-point scale rather than a 4.0-scale GPA and the scheme sets no IELTS figure, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf', source_url = 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf', application_url = 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (cleanup pass 105). The previously stored URL (oia.hanyang.ac.kr/scholarships) resolves to a page that presents the Hanyang International Excellence Awards for already-enrolled students rather than HISP. The terms above were read first-hand from Hanyang OIA's official 2024 Spring Admission Guideline for International Students (Graduate), fetched 2026-10-26: section 08 'Scholarships for International Students' sets out HISP-Graduate (qualification GPA 80+ on the 100 scale; HISP 100%/70%/50% tiers; Master 4 / Ph.D 4 / MA-Ph.D 6 semesters excluding extended study and research registration; retention GPA 3.0; selection during admission with no separate application; 100-scale GPA certificate mandatory; grantee numbers vary by semester; no combining with other on-campus scholarships). The undergraduate period (freshmen 8 semesters, transfers 4) follows Hanyang's undergraduate admission guidelines. Reliability 9 (not 10): the most recent full guideline read is the 2024 one - Hanyang re-issues the guideline each semester (the OIA site currently advertises the 2027 Spring guideline), so tier terms should be re-confirmed against the current-semester guideline at application time. award_amount NULL with award_currency KRW and period/basis 'variable' (a percentage waiver stores no money amount; same convention as verified records 451/851). deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (admission-linked; Spring/Fall) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 477 synced; source 2534 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official guideline. Future work may split out the separate Engineering & Science and Language Proficiency scholarships seen in the same guideline after individual verification.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = 'KRW', award_period = 'variable', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Merit-based tuition waiver', tuition_coverage = 'HISP 100%: 100% reduction in tuition and admission fees. HISP 70%: 70% reduction in tuition. HISP 50%: 50% reduction in tuition. Periods (2024 guideline): graduate Master 4, Ph.D 4 and combined MA-Ph.D 6 semesters; undergraduate freshmen 8 semesters (transfers 4).', english_requirements = 'A Korean proficiency standard (TOPIK Level 4 or above, Hanyang IIE Level 4, TOPIK Speaking Level 4 or TOPIK iBT Level 4) must be satisfied to begin the degree program - accepted students below it take a leave of absence first, with exemptions (e.g. English-track majors, supervisor exemption letters); HISP itself sets no IELTS cutoff.', required_documents = $j$["Hanyang international admission application (HISP is selected during the admission process - no separate application)","Certificate of GPA converted to the 100 scale or percentage (mandatory for HISP eligibility)","Diplomas and academic transcripts, apostille or consular verified where required"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Spring (March) and Fall (September) intakes; HISP grantees are selected during the admission process - no separate application (only documents submitted in the official application period count)"}]$json$ WHERE id = 452;

-- 453: POSTECH Graduate TA/RA Scholarship (rel 9)
UPDATE scholarships SET title = 'POSTECH Graduate TA/RA Scholarship', provider = 'Pohang University of Science and Technology (POSTECH)', coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend', amount_usd_value = 0, deadline = 'No separate scholarship deadline: TA/RA scholarship support is arranged through the admitting department and laboratory on POSTECH graduate admission (Spring and Fall intakes).', deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL, degree_levels = $j$["Master's","PhD"]$j$, eligible_majors = $j$["All"]$j$, eligible_countries = '[]', min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL, financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true, description = $desc$POSTECH supports its graduate students primarily through the Graduate TA/RA Scholarship, the assistantship-based scholarship that forms the core of the university's financial-aid system for enrolled Master's and doctoral students (POSTECH publishes no scheme officially named a 'Graduate Fellowship'). Under the 2026 regular rates, the monthly support totals KRW 1,850,000 for Master's students (KRW 884,000 toward tuition plus KRW 966,000 in living allowance) and KRW 2,200,000 for Ph.D. students (KRW 884,000 plus KRW 1,316,000). Students receive at least the basic scholarship in their first semester; from the second semester the amount is adjusted according to the graduate student's achievements. Actual amounts differ by laboratory and supervising professor, and payment is made monthly (on the 25th, to the student's account). Beyond these regular TA/RA payments, POSTECH's financial-aid framework also includes research and project-linked assistantships and various fellowships and grants, so a student's total package depends on their department and lab.$desc$, requirements = $req$Open to students enrolled in POSTECH graduate programs (Master's, Ph.D. and integrated courses), international students included; support is arranged through the admitting department/laboratory rather than by a separate scholarship application round. At least the basic scholarship is provided in the first semester and achievement-based operation applies from the second semester. The financial-aid page publishes no entry GPA or IELTS cutoff for the TA/RA scholarship, so min_gpa/min_ielts are not recorded.$req$, website_url = 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/', source_url = 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/', application_url = 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/', recurrence = 'annual', application_status = 'upcoming', verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 9, is_active = true, last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(), notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (cleanup pass 105). The previously stored URL (admission.postech.ac.kr/intl/grad/fellowship) returns 404 and POSTECH publishes no scheme named 'POSTECH Graduate Fellowship' - its graduate financial-aid page classifies support into fellowship, assistantship (the core system) and other grants, and the flagship support for enrolled graduate students is the TA/RA Scholarship. The record was therefore rewritten into that real scheme (identity step, reliability 9) from POSTECH Graduate Admissions' official Financial Aid page fetched 2026-10-26: the 2026 regular monthly table (Master's KRW 1,850,000 = tuition 884,000 + living 966,000; Ph.D. KRW 2,200,000 = 884,000 + 1,316,000), at least the basic scholarship in the first semester with achievement-based operation from the second, lab/advisor-dependent amounts, and monthly payment on the 25th were all read first-hand. 2026 regular rates are stated as such and are subject to change. award_amount NULL (variable): rates differ by degree and laboratory/advisor. deadline_date NULL/'not_published' (granted through the department/lab on admission; Spring/Fall) with the pattern in rounds; status 'upcoming'. min_gpa/min_ielts NULL. Previous record held the scheme at reliability 4 with no values read. university_scholarships row 478 synced; source 2594 repointed from the bare domain to the fetched official page. Future work may add the Ruth L. Satter Scholarship (Asian female graduate students) and the POSCO Global Scholarship seen on the same page after individual verification of nationality eligibility.$note$, award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = 'month', award_basis = 'variable', living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = 'Monthly TA/RA assistantship support - tuition component + living allowance (2026 regular rates: Master''s total KRW 1,850,000/month; Ph.D. total KRW 2,200,000/month; varies by laboratory)', tuition_coverage = 'Monthly tuition component of KRW 884,000 is included in the 2026 TA/RA totals (KRW 1,850,000/month Master''s; KRW 2,200,000/month Ph.D.), alongside living allowances of KRW 966,000 and KRW 1,316,000 respectively; at least the basic scholarship in the first semester, achievement-based thereafter.', english_requirements = 'English requirements are those of POSTECH graduate admission; the financial-aid page publishes no separate IELTS cutoff for the TA/RA scholarship.', required_documents = $j$["POSTECH graduate admission application (TA/RA support is arranged through the admitting department/laboratory)","Degree certificates and academic transcripts"]$j$, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = $json$[{"pattern":"Granted through the admitting department/laboratory on POSTECH graduate admission (Spring and Fall intakes); at least the basic scholarship in the first semester, then achievement-based each semester"}]$json$ WHERE id = 453;

-- 135: retired (composite of distinct SNU programs; directory title)
UPDATE scholarships SET is_active = false, application_status = 'closed', award_amount = NULL, award_currency = NULL, award_period = NULL, award_basis = NULL, living_allowance = NULL, funding_type = NULL, tuition_coverage = NULL, english_requirements = NULL, required_documents = NULL, expected_opening_period = NULL, expected_deadline_period = NULL, rounds = NULL, notes = $note$Retired on 2026-10-26 after official-source review: this entry conflated two different SNU schemes under one composite title - no single SNU award named 'Global Scholarship Program (GSF)' exists. The previously stored URL (oia.snu.ac.kr/page/scholarship_graduate.php) returns 404, and SNU's live graduate-scholarships pages (en.snu.ac.kr/admission/graduate/scholarships/before_application, fetched 2026-10-26) list distinct, separately-named programs for international graduate applicants on one directory page: the SNU President Fellowship (for teaching staff of major universities in developing countries admitted as PhD students; full tuition for up to 6 semesters plus a monthly stipend, airfare and insurance), the Graduate Scholarship for Foreign Students (GSFS; full tuition for 4 semesters plus a monthly stipend, with an eligible-country list that changes each semester), the Overseas Koreans Scholarship, and the Korean Government Scholarship Program route at SNU (the GKS program itself is already listed separately as scholarship 843). The similarly-named 'Global Scholarship (GS)' appears in SNU notices as a different, after-admission scheme for enrolled students selected through home institutions, which is also not the stored record. A directory or composite of distinct programs is not a single scholarship, and the standing rule for this cleanup forbids rewriting one row into an unrelated scheme, so the record is retired instead. Kept for audit only; not a discoverable scholarship. university_scholarships row 566 withdrawn; source 2618 repointed to the fetched official graduate-scholarships directory page. Follow-up candidates for a later additions batch after individual verification: the SNU President Fellowship and the GSFS (eligibility of Uzbek applicants to be confirmed per semester).$note$, last_updated_at = now() WHERE id = 135;

-- sources: repoint exclusive bare-domain sources to the fetched official pages
UPDATE sources SET url = CASE id WHEN 2618 THEN 'https://en.snu.ac.kr/admission/graduate/scholarships/before_application' WHEN 2549 THEN 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship' WHEN 2775 THEN 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do' WHEN 2556 THEN 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html' WHEN 2534 THEN 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf' WHEN 2594 THEN 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/' ELSE url END, title = CASE id WHEN 2618 THEN 'Graduate Scholarships (Before Application) - Seoul National University admissions' WHEN 2549 THEN 'KAIST Scholarship - KAIST International Graduate Admissions' WHEN 2775 THEN 'Special Scholarships for International Students - Yonsei Graduate School' WHEN 2556 THEN 'KU Graduate School Scholarship for International Students - Korea University' WHEN 2534 THEN '2024 Spring Admission Guideline for International Students (Graduate) - Hanyang University OIA' WHEN 2594 THEN 'Financial Aid (Graduate) - POSTECH Graduate Admissions' ELSE title END, domain = CASE id WHEN 2618 THEN 'en.snu.ac.kr' WHEN 2549 THEN 'admission.kaist.ac.kr' WHEN 2775 THEN 'graduate.yonsei.ac.kr' WHEN 2556 THEN 'graduate2.korea.ac.kr' WHEN 2534 THEN 'oia.hanyang.ac.kr' WHEN 2594 THEN 'adm-g.postech.ac.kr' ELSE domain END, accessed_at = now(), is_verified = true WHERE id IN (2618,2549,2775,2556,2534,2594);

-- university_scholarships: 5 synced (527, 513, 514, 477, 478) + 1 withdrawn (566)
UPDATE university_scholarships SET scholarship_name = CASE id WHEN 566 THEN 'Seoul National University Global Scholarship Program (GSF) (retired: composite of distinct SNU programs)' WHEN 527 THEN 'KAIST Scholarship for International Graduate Students' WHEN 513 THEN 'Yonsei Global Leader Fellowship' WHEN 514 THEN 'Korea University Global Leader Scholarship (Graduate)' WHEN 477 THEN 'Hanyang International Scholarship Program (HISP)' WHEN 478 THEN 'POSTECH Graduate TA/RA Scholarship' ELSE scholarship_name END, availability_status = CASE WHEN id = 566 THEN 'No' ELSE availability_status END, funding_type = CASE id WHEN 566 THEN 'Retired directory/composite entry (2026-10-26)' WHEN 527 THEN 'Full tuition + national health insurance + monthly stipend (KGPS/KPS tiers)' WHEN 513 THEN 'Full entrance & tuition + stipend' WHEN 514 THEN '100% entrance & tuition + living support (Type A, first semester); 60%/65% tuition (Types B/C)' WHEN 477 THEN 'Merit-based tuition waiver (50%/70%/100%)' WHEN 478 THEN 'Tuition component + living allowance via TA/RA assistantship' ELSE funding_type END, max_scholarship = CASE id WHEN 566 THEN 'No single award of this name: SNU graduate page lists distinct programs (President Fellowship, GSFS, Overseas Koreans, GKS)' WHEN 527 THEN 'Full tuition and health insurance plus a research-dependent monthly stipend; KGPS KRW 1,000,000/month x 4 semesters, KPS KRW 300,000/month x 8 semesters' WHEN 513 THEN 'Full entrance and tuition fees plus a Graduate School stipend for 4 semesters (6 for joint degrees)' WHEN 514 THEN 'Type A: 100% entrance and tuition fee waiver + KRW 500,000/month living support for 4 months (first semester)' WHEN 477 THEN '100% reduction in tuition and admission fees (HISP 100% tier); graduate Master/PhD 4 semesters, undergraduate freshmen 8 semesters' WHEN 478 THEN '2026 regular totals: PhD KRW 2,200,000/month (tuition 884,000 + living 1,316,000); Master KRW 1,850,000/month' ELSE max_scholarship END, covers_tuition = CASE id WHEN 527 THEN true WHEN 513 THEN true WHEN 514 THEN true WHEN 477 THEN true WHEN 478 THEN true ELSE covers_tuition END, covers_living_expenses = CASE id WHEN 527 THEN true WHEN 513 THEN true WHEN 514 THEN true WHEN 477 THEN false WHEN 478 THEN true ELSE covers_living_expenses END, official_url = CASE id WHEN 527 THEN 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship' WHEN 513 THEN 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do' WHEN 514 THEN 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html' WHEN 477 THEN 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf' WHEN 478 THEN 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/' ELSE official_url END, source_url = CASE id WHEN 527 THEN 'https://admission.kaist.ac.kr/intl-graduate/FinancialSupport/Scholarship/KAISTScholarship' WHEN 513 THEN 'https://graduate.yonsei.ac.kr/graduate_en/scholar/foreigner_scholar.do' WHEN 514 THEN 'https://graduate2.korea.ac.kr/scholarship/scholarships.html' WHEN 477 THEN 'https://oia.hanyang.ac.kr/files/attach/filebox/2024/01/2024-1_graduate_en.pdf' WHEN 478 THEN 'https://adm-g.postech.ac.kr/ENG/graduate-info/support-policy/' ELSE source_url END, verification_status = CASE WHEN id = 566 THEN 'withdrawn' ELSE 'verified' END, last_verified_at = now() WHERE id IN (566,527,513,514,477,478);
